rxvt-unicode is a customizable terminal emulator forked from rxvt.
Features of rxvt-unicode include international language support through
Unicode, transparency, the ability to display multiple font types and
support for Perl extensions.

This package adds text shaping with harfbuzz, 24-bit colour, wide
glyphs (drawn over the next cell instead of clipped), improved font
rendering and OSC 110/111/112 colour reset, and reverts line rewrapping
to the 9.30 behaviour. Scrollbars, fading, pixbuf backgrounds and
startup notification are disabled.

Resources added:

	ligatures (-lig/+lig): shape each run of text with harfbuzz
	  so ligatures and contextual alternates from the font are
	  used; only Xft fonts are shaped. Default off.

	fontFeatures (-ff): comma separated list of OpenType features
	  in harfbuzz syntax (liga, -dlig, ss01=1). Default
	  liga,calt,dlig.

	matcher.join-wrapped: join URLs split across rows by programs
	  that wrap on their own. Default off.

It conflicts with the x11/rxvt-unicode package.
